WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.010
MAGDA JARY: Welcome to the
certification preparation

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.950
Professional Security Engineer
and Professional Network

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.750
Engineer certification.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.390
My name is Magda, and
I'm the global lead

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:23.090
for the Google Cloud
Certification and Digital

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.950
Badges Go-to-Market team.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.460
And joining me today is Cori
Peele, customer engineer

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.390
at Google Cloud.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.770
Let's take a look
at our agenda today.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:36.180
First, we'll review the
certification benefits.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.470
Then we'll review the learning
resources and the Google Cloud

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.570
Certification's portfolio.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:45.990
We'll then talk with Cori
about her certification

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:48.150
and preparation journey.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:52.330
And then we'll recap with
the additional resources.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:58.600
So let's get started with
the certification benefits.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.960
First of all, cloud
skills are really

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.330
critical to enabling
customer success

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.040
and fueling our ecosystem.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.850
The job posting looking
for cloud skills

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:13.590
grew over 40% between
the first quarter of 2019

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:17.000
and the first quarter of 2021.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.230
Secondly, over 90%
of IT leaders expect

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:25.430
to expand cloud services in
the next one to three years,

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:30.170
but over 80% of them identified
a lack of internal skills

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:34.920
and knowledge as the top
barriers to cloud success.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.580
And then lastly, the
Google Cloud skills

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:40.130
are particularly in
high demand, commanding

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:44.240
the top two paying IT
certifications in 2021

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:44.885
in the US.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:51.350
We also love to hear from
our community about the Cloud

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:53.720
Certification Program impact.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:58.220
78% of our survey respondents
feel more confident

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:00.410
in their professional future.

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:05.330
82% can prove cloud skills
competency to recruiters.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:09.090
83% feel that their
resume is more attractive.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:16.450
And then finally, 85% feel
more confident in cloud skills.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:17.830
Here are some of
the benefits you

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:21.190
can enjoy by joining the
certification community

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:23.500
and achieving your
certification.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:27.160
First, you distinguish yourself
with a Google Cloud Certified

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.320
badge and a certificate.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:32.950
You also receive exclusive
Google Cloud Certified swag

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.050
for our professional exams.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:38.200
You can network and exchange
ideas in the Google Cloud

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.060
Certified community.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:45.730
And you also receive special
recognition at select events.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:48.340
Let's review some of
the learning resources

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:51.070
and our Google Cloud
certifications.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:55.700
Here are some of
the modalities that

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:59.930
really help us build skills for
the future with Google Cloud

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:05.300
Learning, starting with the
instructor-led format delivered

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.860
by our authorized
training partners.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:12.970
Then we also have a modality
of the on-demand training

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:19.010
so you can learn any time by the
use of the on-demand content.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:21.680
The third piece is
really the hands-on labs

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.620
and is really all about
learning by doing.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.110
So you can practice
there directly

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:29.450
with Google Cloud technologies.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:33.200
And lastly, our Google
Cloud Certified program

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:37.760
that really provides a framework
and benchmark for success

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.290
in core job roles.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:45.130
Our exams are proficiency
and role-based

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:49.460
and provide you a
benchmark for success.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:52.880
And let's take a look at the
overall portfolio of our Google

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.680
Cloud certifications.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:58.640
You'll notice we have the exams
at the professional level, as

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.370
well as our associate
cloud engineer,

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:04.670
and the very recently
launched cloud digital leader.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:08.000
This final one is for
the business audience.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.880
Otherwise, our associate
and professional exams

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:14.060
are all job role-based
and really cater

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.830
to the technical audience.

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:19.700
Today in our session, we focus
on the professional cloud

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:22.730
security engineer and the
professional cloud network

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:25.180
engineer.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:28.500
So let's start with the
review of the readiness path

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:34.800
for the networking and
security network engineer role.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.760
You can notice the resources
in the Learn section,

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:42.600
then some hands-on practice
resources with skill badges,

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.450
and then some additional
preparation resources.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.790
You can find all
of these resources

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:51.930
on our external
training website.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:55.260
Specifically reviewing the
professional cloud network

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:58.530
engineer role, let's really
have a better understanding

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:01.110
what this role is really about.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.450
A professional cloud
network engineer

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:07.860
implements and manages network
architectures in Google Cloud.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:11.550
This individual may work on
networking or cloud teams

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:15.090
with architects who design
cloud infrastructure.

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:19.620
The cloud network engineer uses
the Google Cloud Console and/or

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:23.010
command-line interface
and leverages experience

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:26.250
with network services,
application, and container

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:30.030
networking, hybrid and
multicloud connectivity,

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:34.200
implementing VPCs and security
for established network

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.750
architectures to
ensure successful cloud

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:38.610
implementations.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:43.350
And you can review our exam
page for further details.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:45.960
On the exam page,
you'll also notice,

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:48.900
what are the core domains
covered by the exam?

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:53.303
And it's all available in the
certification exam guide that's

00:05:53.303 --> 00:05:54.345
available on the website.

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:01.010
Likewise, let's review
the preparation path

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:03.760
for the security
engineer certification.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:06.840
You can note that the
learning resources, trainings,

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.690
then in the practice section,
the hands-on labs and skill

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:13.840
badges, some of the
preparation resources,

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:19.240
like sample questions, and then
finally, the certification.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:23.680
So likewise, who is the
professional security engineer?

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:26.140
This person enables
organizations

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:31.360
to design and implement a secure
infrastructure on Google Cloud.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:34.300
Through an understanding
of security best practices

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.980
and industry security
requirements,

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:39.460
this individual
designs, develops,

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:42.700
and manages a secure
infrastructure leveraging

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:45.370
Google security technologies.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:48.280
The cloud security professional
should be proficient

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:50.620
in all aspects of
cloud security,

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:54.190
including managing identity
and access management,

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:57.040
defining organizational
structure and policies,

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:01.090
using Google technologies
to provide data protection,

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:03.850
configuring network
security defenses,

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:07.000
collecting and analyzing
Google Cloud logs,

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:11.080
managing incident reports, and
demonstrating an understanding

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:13.330
of regulatory concerns.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.700
All of this
available on our exam

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:20.110
website, including the detailed
domains that the security

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:23.070
engineer exam covers.

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:26.610
So very briefly, a little bit
more information about these

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:27.580
exams.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.940
They are two hours
long, multiple choice,

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:31.350
and multiple select.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.980
There are no prerequisites.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:36.600
However, we strongly recommend
you have around three years

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:40.890
of industry experience,
including a year, at least,

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:44.370
of hands-on GCP knowledge.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:47.950
So with this, I'm really
delighted to welcome Cori.

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:48.973
Hello, Cori.

00:07:48.973 --> 00:07:49.890
CORI PEELE: Hi, Magda.

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:51.200
How are you today?

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.200
MAGDA JARY: Really good.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.370
Great to see you.

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:56.700
So we would love to get
your insights, expertise

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.310
on the topic of the security
and network engineer

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.570
certifications.

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:03.210
So if you could
start with letting

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:06.270
us know about your role
in some of the projects

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:08.210
you are working on.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.290
CORI PEELE: Yes, thanks.

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:12.110
I'm a customer engineer
with Google Cloud.

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:15.410
And in this role, I'm able
to work with customers

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:18.470
to understand their
business requirements,

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:22.190
some of the things they may
want to do to maybe transform

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:24.770
their industry, and
I work with them

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.890
to understand how they
can accomplish some

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:31.190
of those goals using
Google Cloud and parts

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:33.530
of Google Cloud's ecosystem.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.840
And in order to do
this, I need to have

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:39.409
a really good understanding
of what we have

00:08:39.409 --> 00:08:41.960
available in terms of features.

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:43.220
But not just that.

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:46.880
It's really focusing on, how
do you solve these business

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:51.620
problems with the right
amount of emphasis

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:56.240
on performance for the right
price at the right time?

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:59.330
And by doing this with
some of my customers--

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:02.630
and some of you may be seeing
some of them speak during

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:03.980
Google Next--

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:09.890
we are able to accomplish
really meaningful and impactful

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:12.770
accomplishments, not
just for the customer,

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:15.620
but also for the
users they serve.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:18.590
And in that way, they
all have a bit of a focus

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:22.560
on improving our overall
experience in the world today.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.655
So it's extremely rewarding.

00:09:24.655 --> 00:09:26.030
MAGDA JARY: That's
great to hear.

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.160
Thank you, Cori.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:30.610
So please tell us about your
certification preparation

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:32.740
experience.

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:33.430
CORI PEELE: Yes.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:37.810
So in my case, I had
several certifications.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:42.730
However, I was focusing
on how to study

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:45.070
where I'm optimizing my time.

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:48.580
Because when you think about
the certification journeys

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:51.370
and you look at the
exam guides, you

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:54.730
will see that there are
certain common recommendations

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:57.490
across networking and security.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:00.760
So having a really
solid understanding

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:03.460
of the foundational
infrastructure

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:06.290
components of Google Cloud
will be the first thing.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:10.540
And so we have the ability to
use instructor-led training

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:14.770
or on-demand training through
Pluralsight or Coursera.

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:19.540
So I mapped out the
courses, and I also

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:22.300
leveraged the
certification paths

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:26.530
that have been outlined by
our certification leads.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:31.810
And so by doing this, I was
able to go through the training

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:34.250
in terms of on-demand training.

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:38.740
I had also mapped
out the questions

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:40.630
that were maybe
giving me some trouble

00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:42.700
when I took the practice exam.

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:45.820
And this is extremely useful,
because the Google Cloud

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:51.490
practice exam gives you not
only an explanation regarding

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:55.120
each answer, but it gives
you links to resources

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:57.080
for further information.

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:59.560
So after doing
that practice exam

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.480
and understanding that
there are other areas

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:05.710
to focus on a bit more, I
was able to really research

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:09.730
and make sure I had a solid
understanding of those topics,

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:10.700
as well.

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:15.520
I also participated in community
activities, where several of us

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.580
are embarking on a
certification journey together.

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:23.380
And this helps, because you're
able to ask questions and also

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:26.510
benefit from
communicating with others.

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:29.650
And so in this case,
once I felt comfortable

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:34.420
that I was able to answer
the questions across all

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:37.000
of the sections
of the exam guide,

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:41.020
then I registered for the
exam and I was able to pass.

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:45.310
So I'm very fortunate to
have several certifications,

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:48.100
including the security
and networking engineer

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:50.108
certifications.

00:11:50.108 --> 00:11:52.150
MAGDA JARY: Wonderful,
and congratulations, Cori.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:53.907
CORI PEELE: Thanks.

00:11:53.907 --> 00:11:55.490
MAGDA JARY: So how
would you encourage

00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:58.940
someone brand new to the
security or network engineering

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:03.440
area to set a goal of
achieving a certification?

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:06.590
CORI PEELE: Yes, I would really
encourage you to think about

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:09.920
how this benefits your
day-to-day activities,

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:14.360
in addition to how it may impact
your company and your growth

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:16.760
in your organization as a whole.

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:21.470
The things you are doing
today in your environment

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:25.430
might be focused on maybe a
couple of different patterns

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.230
and a few different
architectures,

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:30.170
based on what you have in
your environment today.

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:32.870
However, in order to
really be prepared

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:35.480
for different types
of challenges,

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:38.780
and to really have a
solid understanding of how

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:42.380
you can apply these
types of technologies

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:45.710
to other business problems,
it's important to have

00:12:45.710 --> 00:12:49.280
a very detailed understanding
and a broad understanding

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:53.970
of a lot of the topics that
are covered in the exam.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:56.240
And so I really would
encourage you to think

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:59.700
about achieving certification.

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:02.670
Think about planning-- and
I would say think of it

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:07.230
in terms of maybe in 12
weeks, so within one quarter.

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:10.980
You may start your studying in
the beginning of the quarter

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:15.210
and then plan to have an
exam taken towards the end.

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:17.460
So that way, you're
able to incorporate

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:21.480
studying for the exam with
all the other things you're

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.440
probably doing at the same time.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:26.370
And so with that
type of structure,

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:28.560
it's fairly reasonable
for you to be

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:33.120
able to really have
that goal established

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.340
and then also achieve the goal.

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:38.010
And don't worry if you
don't pass the first time.

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:41.010
You have the ability
to retake the exam.

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:45.810
So again, the focus
on establishing

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:49.950
that type of target goal, and
then planning your schedule

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:53.670
accordingly so you can
meet that timeline.

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:56.220
MAGDA JARY: Thank you, and
thank you for all the tips.

00:13:56.220 --> 00:14:01.020
Cori, could you review some of
the synergies between security

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:03.960
and networking in Google Cloud?

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:06.900
CORI PEELE: Yes, and there
are a lot of synergies.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:10.260
And actually, when you think
about what the cloud is,

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:14.730
we are thinking about the
resources that are networked.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:19.260
And so network security
is very important.

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:22.110
And you will find that there
are networking and security

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:23.970
topics on both exams.

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:28.560
So one really important
perspective we have at Google

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:32.490
is to think about
a zero-trust model.

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:36.090
We've published a white
paper called Beyond Corp.

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:39.390
And this is just a
different way of thinking

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:43.440
about managing security and
network security for those who

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:48.600
are used to the world where
you have a demilitarized zone,

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:52.590
and you're allowing
communications across the board

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:54.540
as soon as someone
has permission

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:55.800
to get into that perimeter.

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:58.170
Well, with zero
trust, this means

00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:01.620
that even though you may
be in the same network,

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:03.430
you do not have access.

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:05.010
So this is, again, nothing--

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:08.790
no access unless
you are granted that

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:12.570
by a policy explicitly
or something where

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.290
you are inheriting it.

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:18.870
So being able to apply
these types of principles

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:22.830
across multiple products in the
security and networking space

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:24.450
will be really important.

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:28.920
Also, it's important to
think about how we approach

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:31.140
open-source software security.

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:33.750
So we have a lot of
different mechanisms

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:38.130
to plan how we are
managing development

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:40.443
and what happens from a
development standpoint.

00:15:40.443 --> 00:15:42.360
But also, when you're
doing additional builds,

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:45.420
there are many other
types of approaches.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:49.530
And so this is something that
you want to really think about,

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:54.630
because the impact of
leveraging open source,

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:58.900
where potentially-- this
doesn't happen that often.

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:02.940
But it has happened where
there may be a bad actor.

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:07.180
And so how do you prevent that
from impacting your business?

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:10.560
So making sure you
have enough awareness

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:16.200
of a lot of the latest practices
and demonstrating competency

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:20.880
to really plan to protect your
organization is important.

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:23.140
Again, protecting
against ransomware.

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:27.250
Ransomware is a problem our
world is dealing with now

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:30.720
and it seems to
be getting worse.

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:34.620
However, we have
tools and products

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:39.450
and processes to help protect
against ransomware and other

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:40.720
types of attacks.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:43.650
So having this type
of knowledge lets

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:46.710
you understand what you may do
on the networking side in terms

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:49.870
of how you're protecting
from that standpoint,

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:52.620
but then also from a security.

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:55.890
And then when people think about
cybersecurity in general, how

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:57.640
do you really approach this?

00:16:57.640 --> 00:17:01.770
And so we have, again, processes
and tools and product offerings

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:03.660
to assist with that.

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:08.460
One major change in
the past several years

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:11.880
has been the shift
from just working

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:15.720
with data centers that
are owned by a company

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:18.690
to a cloud infrastructure.

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:23.369
And then now you actually
have several approaches

00:17:23.369 --> 00:17:26.160
where you're thinking about
multicloud and hybrid cloud.

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:31.590
So your approach to security
across all of these boundaries,

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:34.080
and then also the
way you approach it--

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:37.680
let's say if you were maybe
monetizing some offerings,

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:42.120
or doing joint ventures and
you have a different definition

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:44.290
of what these boundaries
actually are--

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:47.190
this becomes something
that can appear

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:49.020
to be fairly complicated.

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:52.110
However, if you are
able to leverage

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:54.960
some of the recommendations
and best practices

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:58.770
from Google Cloud, you'll have
an understanding of the way

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:03.090
to approach this so that your
company and organization will

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:06.750
be able to be really flexible as
different demands and business

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:09.000
models emerge in the future.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:13.500
And then really thinking about
cybersecurity and resilience,

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:16.300
cyber-resilience is
extremely important.

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:23.040
And when you are thinking about
the broad spectrum of security

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:26.080
and networking and how
it's addressed together,

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:29.490
it's really providing
you with the capabilities

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:32.620
to address these
real-world problems.

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:35.850
So I really recommend
anyone who--

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:37.770
again, if you already
have a certification,

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:41.400
or maybe you're someone who's a
manager of people who are doing

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:44.340
more of the hands-on
tasks, it's still

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:47.820
useful to think about
getting these certifications,

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:49.740
because these
certifications focus on,

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:55.220
how do you approach the design
to meet a certain business need

00:18:55.220 --> 00:18:57.740
or to address certain problems?

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:00.740
And it's not focused
on just tasks.

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:04.040
So by having a really
great understanding

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:08.000
of how you approach the design
of security and networking

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.290
will really be very beneficial.

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:15.420
So yeah, and Magda, thanks for
